  "notes": "GAAP (modified accrual) per the combined Statement of Governmental Fund Revenues, Expenditures and Changes in Fund Balances and Statement of Activities (p2, original report p7, gained in the v7 re-trim). Receipts/disbursements and fund balances (433,550 / 403,515) from its Total governmental funds column (General + Construction; General Fund beginning balance is negative, -24,851); the reconciling-items and Statement of Activities columns are not used (net position 3,312,661 beginning / 2,719,469 ending; depreciation 246,301 appears only there). Warrants issued 337,523 + bond issuance 1,340,000 = debt_proceeds 1,677,523 (computed). Roll-forward: 433,550+178,349-1,885,907+1,677,523=403,515. Collection fees are printed as a negative revenue line and kept so (property tax, review). Placement fees and bond issue costs as debt service fees. Previously (old trim had only Schedule 1) receipts/disbursements came from Schedule 1 and its budgetary fund balances 460,808 / 420,029 were used as beginning/ending cash; those Schedule 1 lines stay in detail (budgetary basis, Actual and budget columns, now p3; Schedule 1 shows bond proceeds 1,286,400 vs 1,340,000 bond issuance on the GAAP statement; outlay actual printed as '---'), and beginning cash is null (no prior-year balance sheet). Read pages 1-3 of 3. Balance sheet from the combined Balance Sheet - Governmental Funds and Statement of Net Position (p1, original report p6, gained in the v8 re-trim), Statement of Net Position column (warrants and bonds split by the printed due dates; accrued interest as accrued liabilities; fund-column deferred revenue and fund balances reconcile to '---' there). ending_cash = Cash on deposit with County Treasurer 91,077 and ending_investments = Investments 330,583 (Total governmental funds column, same as the Statement of Net Position column)."
